{"name":"Crystal Falls","hex":"#e1e6f2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Crystal Falls","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A community in West Nipissing, Ontario, Canada.","A ghost town in Quebec, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Crystal_Falls"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cristal Falls (Brazil)","blocks":[{"text":"Cristal Falls is a waterfall in the Cristal Mountains of Brazil. It is located in the city of Santo Antônio do Rio Abaixo in the state of Minas Gerais. It is approximately 20 m (66 ft) high."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Cachoeira_do_Cristal.JPG/330px-Cachoeira_do_Cristal.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cristal_Falls_(Brazil)"},{"title":"West Nipissing","blocks":[{"text":"West Nipissing is a municipality in Northeastern Ontario, Canada, on Lake Nipissing in the Nipissing District. It was formed on January 1, 1999, with the amalgamation of seventeen and a half former towns, villages, townships and unorganized communities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Sturgeon_Falls_Ontario.JPG/330px-Sturgeon_Falls_Ontario.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Nipissing"},{"title":"Crystal","blocks":[{"text":"A crystal or crystalline solid is a solid material whose constituents are arranged in a highly ordered microscopic structure, forming a crystal lattice that extends in all directions. In addition, macroscopic single crystals are usually identifiable by their geometrical shape, consisting of flat faces with specific, characteristic orientations. The scientific study of crystals and crystal formation is known as crystallography. The process of crystal formation via mechanisms of crystal growth is called crystallization or solidification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki